Prometheus MCP server: query and manage a running Prometheus{{ if .Backend }} ({{ .Backend }} backend){{ end }} instance via PromQL, discovery/metadata endpoints, and management APIs.{{ if hasTool "docs_search" }} Official Prometheus docs are embedded (docs_search tool, prometheus://docs resources).{{ end }}{{ if .Runbooks }} Guided runbooks are embedded (runbooks_list tool; also exposed as prompts and skill:// resources).{{ end }}

Core rules:
- Use the tools to fetch live data; never invent query results or answer from assumed state.
- Never assume a metric or label name exists: discover with label_values (label="__name__"), metric_metadata, or series, then build queries from verified names.
- Keep results small: aggregate and filter in PromQL, and cap output with the truncation_limit parameter that query and list tools accept.
{{- if hasTool "docs_search" }}
- If you are unsure how something in Prometheus works (PromQL, configuration, internals), try docs_search before searching externally.
{{- end }}
- ALWAYS confirm with the user before calling destructive or state-changing tools (see tool descriptions).
{{- if hasTool "delete_series" }}
{{- if .TSDBAdminToolsEnabled }}
- TSDB admin tools also require the Prometheus flag --web.enable-admin-api; calls fail if it is not set.
{{- else }}
- TSDB admin tools (delete_series, clean_tombstones, snapshot) are disabled on this server; do not call them unless it is restarted with --dangerous.enable-tsdb-admin-tools.
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- if .Backend }}
- This server is configured for the "{{ .Backend }}" backend; the toolset is tailored accordingly.
{{- else }}
- Any Prometheus-API-compatible backend (Thanos, Mimir, ...) may be behind this server; use build_info to identify it.
{{- end }}
{{- if .Runbooks }}

Runbooks -- read with runbooks_read or the skill://<name>/SKILL.md resource, and follow when a task matches:
